S0. THE MASTER FORMULA a0_eff/a0 = v_orb/v_rel -- derived symbolically, not assumed
========================================================================================================
  [OK  ] Theorem 8 reproduced symbolically: w/x = c/v exactly, identically in Omega, v and a0
  [OK  ] the c cancels: w_A = Omega*v_rel/a0 (no c left)
  [OK  ] if v_rel = v_orb the repair is EXACT on circles -- Theorem 8's c/v gap closes identically
  [OK  ] a0_eff = a0 * v_orb/v_rel exactly (sympy: a_0*v/v_rel)
  [OK  ] v_rel -> 0 (a co-moving/velocity-dragged frame) DIVERGES a0_eff -- catastrophic, not small
  [OK  ] v_rel -> infinity kills a0_eff -> 0, i.e. restores Newton -- the other failure mode
  [OK  ] the alpha=2 closure is g_bar = A**2/sqrt(A**2 + a_0**2), which squares EXACTLY to the biquadratic A^4 - g^2 A^2 - g^2 a0^2 = 0
  [OK  ] the closed form A^2 = (g^2/2)(1+sqrt(1+4a0^2/g^2)) solves that biquadratic EXACTLY
  [OK  ] and it is the RIGHT branch: max relative residual of the closure over g_bar spanning 20 decades = 2.67e-51 at 50 dps
  [OK  ] negative control: the retired alpha=1 inversion does NOT solve the alpha=2 closure

========================================================================================================
S1. WELL-DEFINEDNESS: does the potential-stationary u exist, and is it unique?
========================================================================================================

  S1a. The rigid-rotation degeneracy Carl flagged -- CONFIRMED, exactly as stated.
  [OK  ] L_u Phi = 0 holds IDENTICALLY for ARBITRARY Omega_f on any static axisymmetric Phi: the potential-stationarity condition alone leaves a 1-parameter rigid-rotation degeneracy
  [OK  ] negative control: with an m=2 bar, Omega_f = 0 still works but generic Omega_f does NOT -- so the degeneracy is a property of axisymmetry, not of the definition

  S1b. Pointwise degeneracy count for a GENERIC time-dependent Phi (the worse obstruction).
  [OK  ] L_u Phi = 0 is 1 equation on 3 components of the frame velocity => solution space is 2-dimensional at EVERY point (nullspace dim = 2 in 200/200 random draws). The scalar condition ALONE is far more degenerate than the axisymmetric Omega_f: any frame velocity tangent to the local equipotential works

  S1c. Does IRROTATIONALITY / hypersurface-orthogonality kill Omega_f? (flat space first)
  [OK  ] curl of the rigid frame field = 2*Omega_f zhat exactly -- vanishes IFF Omega_f = 0
  [OK  ] Frobenius 3-form component T_[t R phi] = -2*Omega_f*R -- exactly -2 R Omega_f
  [OK  ] so in flat space HSO forces Omega_f = 0 UNIQUELY -- and HSO is the SAME condition the framework already needs to kill vector modes and keep u PASSIVE (not an extra assumption)

  S1d. With a ROTATING source (g_tphi != 0) the answer changes: the HSO solution is the ZAMO.
  [OK  ] general stationary-axisymmetric Frobenius: T_[t R phi] = A d_R B - B d_R A = A^2 d_R(B/A), so HSO <=> B/A = const == -k
  [OK  ] the k=0 branch is the ZAMO: Omega = -g_tphi/g_phiphi = -g_tphi(R, z)/g_phiphi(R, z)
  [OK  ] a 1-parameter family of HSO congruences DOES exist, Omega(k) = (-k*g_tt(R, z) - g_tphi(R, z))/(k*g_tphi(R, z) + g_phiphi(R, z)); k=0 recovers the ZAMO
  [OK  ] but the k-leaves are t = k*phi + const, and phi -> phi + 2pi shifts t by 2*pi*k: the time function is MULTIVALUED unless k = 0. AZIMUTHAL PERIODICITY therefore fixes k = 0 and the frame is UNIQUE = the ZAMO. This is the load-bearing uniqueness argument
      SCOPE, stated so it is not overread: this uniqueness is WITHIN the stationary
      axisymmetric congruence ansatz u^mu ~ (1, 0, Omega(R,z), 0). S1b already showed the
      bare scalar condition is 2-parameter degenerate pointwise, so uniqueness is bought by
      the ansatz + HSO + periodicity together, NOT by potential-stationarity alone.
  [OK  ] weak-field equatorial g_tphi = -2GJ/(c^2 R), g_phiphi = R^2 => Omega_ZAMO = 1.33486e-10*J/(R**3*c**2) = the standard Lense-Thirring dragging rate (quantified in S4)

  S1e. QUANTIFIED: what the residual freedom would do to the RAR if it were NOT removed.
   Omega_f / Omega_orb  v_rel/v_orb    a0_eff/a0  |dlog a0| dex
                     0            1            1              0
                 1e-06     0.999999            1    4.34295e-07
                 0.001        0.999        1.001    0.000434512
                   0.1          0.9      1.11111      0.0457575
                   0.5          0.5            2        0.30103
                   0.9          0.1           10              1
                  0.99         0.01          100              2
  [OK  ] if Omega_f were free the induced a0 spread is UNBOUNDED (diverges at Omega_f = Omega_orb). It exceeds the 0.2232 dex budget for Omega_f/Omega > 0.402 -- NOT already at 0.1, where it is only 0.0458 dex (an earlier draft of this line overstated it and is corrected here). Since Omega_f is a FREE FUNCTION with no reason to sit below 0.402, the degeneracy WOULD be fatal; removing it is not cosmetic

