========================================================================================================
S3. IS a0 = c H_Lambda / Z PRESERVED when u is boosted relative to comoving?
========================================================================================================
  Carl's expectation was O(v^2/c^2) ~ 1e-6 and harmless. The answer is BETTER than that:
  for a GEODESIC observer the shift is EXACTLY zero, by dS invariance. Both shown.

  S3a. The boost is an ISOMETRY of dS (embedding-space check, symbolic).
  [OK  ] L^T eta L = eta exactly => the boost is in SO(4,1) = the dS isometry group, so it maps the hyperboloid X.X = 1/H^2 to itself and maps geodesics to geodesics
  [OK  ] the Gibbons-Hawking temperature T = H/2pi depends on H alone, and H is the invariant radius of the hyperboloid; Bunch-Davies is dS-invariant => EVERY geodesic observer sees the SAME T. a0 = c H_Lambda/Z is therefore boost-invariant EXACTLY, not to O(v^2/c^2)

  S3b. A constant-comoving-momentum (i.e. boosted) worldline in dS is GEODESIC: proper
       acceleration identically zero, so the dS-Unruh T = sqrt(H^2 + a_prop^2/c^2)/2pi is
       unshifted. Checked by explicit 4-acceleration, 1+1 dS (a = e^{Ht}).
  [OK  ] 4-acceleration of the boosted (constant-p) dS worldline is EXACTLY zero in both components => it is a geodesic => T = H/2pi with no correction of any order in beta
  [OK  ] control: comoving (p=0) is the p->0 limit of the same family, also geodesic (consistency)

  S3c. The PESSIMISTIC alternative -- treat the boost as a naive Doppler shift of a fixed
       bath (i.e. pretend dS invariance fails completely). mpmath 50 dps because gamma-1 is
       a difference of nearly-equal numbers.
  v_drag [km/s]        beta       gamma-1   dex(gamma)  dipole beta dex   vs budget
          100.0  3.3356e-04    5.5633e-08   2.4161e-08       1.4484e-04      1541.0x
          300.0  1.0007e-03    5.0069e-07   2.1745e-07       4.3438e-04       513.8x
          620.0  2.0681e-03    2.1385e-06   9.2875e-07       8.9724e-04       248.8x
         1000.0  3.3356e-03    5.5633e-06   2.4161e-06       1.4462e-03       154.3x
  [OK  ] even the maximally pessimistic DIPOLE estimate (linear in beta, v = 1000 km/s) gives 1.446e-03 dex, 154x inside the 0.2232 dex budget. So item 3 is safe on BOTH readings: exactly zero if dS invariance is used, and still negligible if it is thrown away

  Both footings, absolute size of the pessimistic shift in a0:
      canonical rho_DE     a0 = 9.3600e-11  ->  delta a0 (dipole, 620 km/s) = 1.9357e-13 m/s^2
      alt rho_total        a0 = 1.1300e-10  ->  delta a0 (dipole, 620 km/s) = 2.3370e-13 m/s^2
  [OK  ] absolute pessimistic shift < 1e-12 m/s^2 on both footings -- five orders below the cluster-scale discrepancies the corpus already carries

