========================================================================================================
S6. EQUIVALENCE PRINCIPLE, MOMENTUM CONSERVATION, and what existing bounds actually reach
========================================================================================================

  S6a. WEP (composition independence): a0_eff = a0 v_orb/v_rel is purely KINEMATIC.
  [OK  ] d a0_eff/d(mass) = d a0_eff/d(composition) = 0 identically => WEP / universality of free fall is preserved EXACTLY. Route A cannot be attacked by Eotvos-type experiments

  S6b. NEWTON'S THIRD LAW in an EXTERNAL frame -- I expected a violation and did not find one.
       Setup: unequal-mass pair whose frame-relative speed is dominated by the COM motion
       v_f, so each body's OWN orbital speed v_i = (m_j/M) v_orb sets its a0_eff.
  [OK  ] the DIMENSIONLESS closure argument a0_eff,i/g_bar,i is IDENTICAL for the two bodies (both equal kappa r^2/G) -- because a0_eff,i ~ m_j and g_bar,i ~ m_j, the same factor
  [OK  ] therefore m_1 A_1 - m_2 A_2 = 0 EXACTLY, for ARBITRARY closure function F: momentum is conserved in the two-body case even with the frame set by an external field. This is a structural cancellation, not a numerical accident -- and it removes a liability I expected
  [OK  ] negative control: a body-independent a0_eff (the ordinary MI prescription) does NOT satisfy the same identity, so the check has real content and is not a tautology
       CAVEAT, stated: this is the TWO-body result. Three-body and internally structured
       cases are NOT tested here and no claim is made about them.

